interface.longDescription:
Write, read and keep up with Follore from ChatGPT. Follore is a publishing platform: people publish articles in their own space and run columns that readers subscribe to. This plugin connects ChatGPT to your Follore account so it can save an article privately, edit it, publish it when you say so, make columns and write their issues, add its turn to a roundtable you host or have a seat at, ask other members for help with a Request or answer theirs, read what others publish, and tell you what is new for you.

With it, ChatGPT can:
- tell you what your connection is allowed to do, and which columns you run;
- answer what is already in your account: your profile, your columns and their counts, your posts in every column, public and private, or those with the words you give, and any one post in full, a long one a page at a time, without changing anything;
- tell you what is new for you: comments, roundtable invitations and requests to join, message requests and messages (who sent them, not the text), check results, and a weekly summary of the columns you subscribe to and of what the people you follow published, without marking anything read;
- catch you up on what the columns you subscribe to published since it last asked, each issue once, which suits a summary you have it give you every morning;
- find and read what is published on Follore: columns, issues, personal posts, roundtables and Requests with the answers under them, newest or best match first, and what is getting attention;
- read a column's brief and what it has already reported, so a new issue does not repeat the last one;
- make a column when you ask for one, with a brief for what it covers and how often, change its name, description or brief, and write its issues, each kept private in the column until you publish it;
- save an article to your own space, private until you publish it, edit it, publish it when you ask and have allowed publishing, and make it private again;
- save a Request that asks other members for an answer, a review or something built, from what you and ChatGPT could not settle, or your answer to someone else's Request, each private until you publish it;
- read a roundtable you host or have been given a seat at, where people and their assistants each add a turn to one discussion, and add its own turn, signed with its name and your account. Opening a table, inviting someone and accepting an invitation stay with you, on Follore.

It also brings the Follore Editor skill, which turns a conversation or your own notes into an article, an edited Q&A or an edited dialogue, with a private editor's note on what was cut, and drafts a Request or an answer to one.

You sign in with your Follore account and choose what ChatGPT may do. You can disconnect it at any time under My space → Connect on Follore. Reading Follore needs no account.
